{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174059-klaives-fetishes","id":174059,"title":"Klaives & Fetishes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-19T06:37:26-07:00","id":174059,"title":"Klaives & Fetishes","content":"In our Sweden game I want to add some Norse feel. I got idea that maybe adding some legendary weapon, just like Viking heroes of Dark Ages, would nicely give this. I will probably make a small quest for players to find ancient burial site of local Uratha hero from centuries before. The problem is - I need more fetish weapons. Is there any larger rooster in some of sourcebooks? Or maybe you got some cool ideas? I look especially for once feeling Norse-like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T06:56:18-07:00","id":174080,"title":"","content":"<b>Lore of the Forsaken</b> has a whole section on Fetishes and Klaives, including charts and tips on building your own. <br /> <br /> This book has all the stuff on Gifts, Rites, Totems, Fetishes......all the spirit magic stuff. Pretty essential to running <b>Forsaken</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T07:23:09-07:00","id":174106,"title":"","content":"Quite an Awesome Book it is, too. I find myself constantly referencing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T07:28:32-07:00","id":174109,"title":"","content":"Here's a klaive for you, off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Gungnir - Level 5 Klaive<br /> In Norse mythology, Gungnir was the spear of Odin, king of the Aesir. According to the legends, the spear was so well balanced that it could strike any target, no matter the strength or skill of the wielder. In the legends of the Uratha, a Storm Lord alpha bound a powerful spirit of war and a great eagle spirit together to create Gungnir - a klaive capable of terrible destruction, capable of unerringly striking its chosen target.<br /> <br /> Gungnir does 4 lethal damage, and grants its wielder +1 Defense in close combat against any combatants who aren't themselves wielding staves, spears or polebased weapons, due to the Klaive's superior reach. By paying a point of Willpower and making a successful Harmony roll to activate the klaive, the wielder may ignore the Defense of one opponent for one strike. Armor and environmental conditions penalize this roll as usual.<br /> Action: Reflexive","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T08:10:00-07:00","id":174142,"title":"","content":"There's a few klaives and the moonklaives (klaives with lune spirits in them) in War Against the Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T13:43:15-07:00","id":183196,"title":"","content":"Looked in to Lore of Forsaken and not found anything real suitable. But prepering for the game I found this awesome graphics.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s6738.chomikuj.pl/ChomikImage.aspx?e=LsedsBf7L-6jM7vi4GM3gUTvMvKYjnL7fwaLtl5K4k__bM182e_z3jXgKJNVpo06cVECFL4nzzoUZ1JYmtYhqIIFO_63UaCHizA4ssVxVl4&amp;pv=2\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b> How could be made this armor? What propoerties could have fetish of her? And what sweet klaive could be made from this battleaxe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-29-2014, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T16:14:46-07:00","id":183311,"title":"","content":"For some reason I feel it's a norn from gw2... Anyway the armor can just be dedicated armor. The axe could be anything. Really up to your imagination. Maybe a spirit of razors for extra sharpness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T23:31:55-07:00","id":183577,"title":"","content":"So the question would be is what armor property would be best to use for Blood Talons Alpha from Viking times? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the looks of it, it's a Plate Armor so <b>GMC</b> rules say it will have 4/2 rating and Strength needed 3. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Add in nice war spirit, what could Uratha get from this?<br /> <br /> I have a problem with Battleaxe in his hands. In <b>GMC</b> only we have this stats:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s7277.chomikuj.pl/ChomikImage.aspx?e=fE6xV_fZC3I0zUmsfuEQJ02An0DCW0gdSlRQirq9nLxVPsVD4XHUaAE5wJtbTtFLNT2h0JfJ2D5pQIaqDE-lnXBMq22RJ5AuYzlU8l_OQGE&amp;pv=2\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Clearly Battleaxe would be between Fire Ax and Chainsaw, so I would propose Damage 4, Initiative -5, The Strength and Availability is tricky - better to make it more useful ( lower Strength and Availability ) and also more common, or more demanding on user ( higher Str and Ava ) but also more extraordinary to find?<br /> <br /> As to proper fetish properties - it was gift from <b>All-Father-Thunder</b>, larger god of storms and protection. So maybe nice electricity damage added to Battleaxe?<br /> <br /> I also have idea for some nice klaive dagger, so could strike and return itself to his owner. Basically <i>Assasin's Creed</i> Throwing Daggers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have 5 Uratha in our pack, and with <i>Gungnir</i>, Plate Armor, Battleaxe and Dagger we have 4 klaives. I assume that our Storm Lords Elodoth will be putted a bit on sideways with this. Maybe some idea of fetish for judge and diplomat character in pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-29-2014, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T17:08:02-07:00","id":188320,"title":"","content":"A viking wouldn't use plate armor. They utilize chain mail and gambesons. Possibly helmets. Plate mail was too expensive for them. I'd also argue it weighs them down and eliminates the purpose of their combat styles. &gt;.&gt; That's me though. Remember the viking age is 793-1050ish.... (whenever Harald Hadrada died really), so not a particularly long period of time. The 'honor' weapon of the viking was a pole axe. Something of a special forces gear, so I'd go with a pole axe over a fantastical battle axe all Tolkien'd out. I would advise it to be built with a speed spirit to accentuate its well roundedness, and advise the player in Pole Axe combat. Leg trips, hooking the blade behind the neck and pulling down, and strikes with what appears to be a small axe head.<br /> <br /> The head has to be small to focus all the kinetic energy into the strike. Makes it god damned deadly. <br /> <br /> &gt;.&gt; Guess what I like to study.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T20:46:29-07:00","id":188463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174059-klaives-fetishes?p=188320#post188320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember the viking age is 793-1050ish.... (whenever Harald Hadrada died really), so not a particularly long period of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would Vikings in that time expand they domain also on North, driving original stterlers off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T22:19:35-07:00","id":188512,"title":"","content":"Eh depends on the peoples and their intentions. The Swedish Vikings known as the Rus became the leaders of what is now russia, interbred and became Slavs within 150 years. Ireland would be a good example of conquering, as would England. The great heathen army kicked ass and took over almost all of England (screw you wessex!) and the people there were allowed to live more or less un-molested. Really depends on who was in charge and what laws were common for what king.<br /> <br /> That said, trying to shoe horn viking culture in with Uratha may not work all too well. Even if they went into an area and settled it doesn't necessarily mean they'll drive the local populace out. And with the new rules on how breeding works it isn't like they're wholly reliant on kin groups anymore. Those sorts of questions work good for werewolf the apocalypse but not so much with forsaken, where it's mostly ideologies and not cultural biases. <br /> <br /> I think culturally, the only real problem with native peoples they had as a people (the norse) was when they Christianized. But that is really par the course. Otherwise they're a rather inclusive welcoming people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T02:29:33-07:00","id":188603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/174059-klaives-fetishes?p=188512#post188512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, trying to shoe horn viking culture in with Uratha may not work all too well. Even if they went into an area and settled it doesn't necessarily mean they'll drive the local populace out. And with the new rules on how breeding works it isn't like they're wholly reliant on kin groups anymore. Those sorts of questions work good for werewolf the apocalypse but not so much with forsaken, where it's mostly ideologies and not cultural biases.<br /> <br /> I think culturally, the only real problem with native peoples they had as a people (the norse) was when they Christianized. But that is really par the course. Otherwise they're a rather inclusive welcoming people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Natives were under guidance of Ursara, werebears, and Uratha come with conflict with them, not natives. But with more Norse culture coming to the land. orginal Lappland traditions were forgotten more and more, with each generation. And after this come also Christanity. It as my original plan at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T01:34:21-07:00","id":190025,"title":"","content":"Yeah but that sorta transition is the course of CENTURIES of work. The original migration era of the Norse religions into the original fertility religions of the time can be viewed (theoretically at any rate) with the battle of the Aesir and Vanir, which some scholars believe to be symbolic of the clashing of two world views. This can be backed by the idea that Tyr was originally the lead God of the pantheon (furthered by the definition of Tyr being -god- and one of Odin's name's being , I may be mispelling this, Hanga-Tyr, or hanging god.) It's looked upon in some circles as a rationalizing of the local peoples for the two world views coming together, with one becoming the dominant force (the germanics/Proto Norse). I would argue that in that situation you would be looking at acculturation over outright out kicking. <br /> <br /> As for the Lap folk, the Saami are one of the few native tribes in the world to retain their religious beliefs and customs, and have a reputation for producing powerful sorcerors and witches in Nordic epics (probably due to their &quot;strange&quot; customs.) Remember almost all of our Norse lore that we know is written by christian scholars some 200+ years after the events happened, so naturally it has a Christian tinge to it, making it look like the take over was damn near universal. It sure wasn't. The only place it appears to be the case was Iceland in 999 where it was more due to the King being a prick and black mailing the 'ruling families' with their children's heads over any actual desire to convert. The law speaker just made the land of one religion to avoid confrontation between the two camps in the future. In other parts of Scandinavia (Sweden in particular) it took till the mid 1300's to fully Christianize. Norway went back and forth between a few kings, with seemingly every other king changing their mind on the matter. <br /> <br /> Would the Blood Talons actually fight these bear people or would they view them with some manner of brutal camaraderie? I'd look into that notion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T05:24:29-07:00","id":192292,"title":"","content":"A really cool, Scandinavian weapon you could use is the swordstaff. It's basically what it sounds like; a broadsword on a stick. Kinda like a European naginata. It is also important to note that the swordstaff still had the parry guard to aid in defence. <br /> It is a cool, big, weapon that never really caught on anywhere else, and it looks brutal enough to look like a good weapon for an Uratha.<br /> <br /> If you want classic viking stuff though you should go for long axes and spears really. There were very few good sword smiths in Scandinavia back in the day, so axes and spears were much more common. If you want fetishes from that actually ARE from that era though, go for swords, they were rare and special, and thus the obvious choice when one made a fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T06:43:44-07:00","id":192343,"title":"","content":"Will use ALL of your ideas - I try to be historic accurate, but Cool of Cool is more important. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Would only benefit from some kind Elodoth fetish. Weren't there been some kind of &quot;Crown of Leading&quot; in the line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T07:23:10-07:00","id":192385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Complete+Werewolf+the+Forsaken\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Complete+Werewolf+the+Forsaken\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Complete+Werewolf+the+Forsaken\" target=\"_blank\"> http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Complete+Werewolf+the+Forsaken </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fetishes are near the bottom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T01:15:05-07:00","id":193277,"title":"","content":"Another item that should be of interest to you is 'cursed items'. Look those up. Not quite fetishes but powerful items in their own right. They may add a flavor to your game that you didn't expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}